      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T02:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are clients who use this property expected to wait after receiving a property change signal that indicates a change in Value but not in UpdatedTime?\n\nIs the sensor app supposed to update both properties atomically?",
      "revId": "5374993b5ee9ad3c1da2bff2215bab1e9ba7945d",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de01bd35_9a628e1b",
        "filename": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000212
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-10T17:09:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If automic updates are possible, then yes thats the most optimal, but I do not believe the current dbus interfaces allows for the updates of two properties automically.\n\nI considered two possibilities:\n1. Service updates UpdatedTime before updating Value -- Risk: client has stale value but thinks it is current with the updatedTime.\n2. Service updates UpdatedTime after updating Value -- Risk: client has current value but might think its stale.\n\nBased on  this I defined the order as (2) since it poses the least risk for the client if they have certain realtime constraints.",
      "parentUuid": "609c255d_155ee837",
      "revId": "5374993b5ee9ad3c1da2bff2215bab1e9ba7945d",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81535ba8_333a02ca",
        "filename": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
